WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:09.696 line:88% align:center
Checkpoint drugs work by releasing the brakes on a T cell — but they help only a minority of patients, because only a handful of those brakes are drugged.

2
00:00:09.696 --> 00:00:12.412 line:88% align:center
So we went looking for the rest, genome-wide.

3
00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:15.188 line:88% align:center
This is Brakepoint, built with Claude Science.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.687 line:88% align:center
Those brakes matter beyond checkpoint therapy — they also throttle engineered CAR-T.

5
00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:23.654 line:88% align:center
So across the genome: which genes are the brakes?

6
00:00:23.654 --> 00:00:28.135 line:88% align:center
And which knockdowns push a human T cell toward a stronger effector state?

7
00:00:28.567 --> 00:00:37.259 line:88% align:center
6 million primary human CD4 T cells, from the Gladstone Institutes.

8
00:00:37.259 --> 00:00:41.929 line:88% align:center
Two donors, out of an intended four.

9
00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:46.029 line:88% align:center
How do you find the brakes in twelve thousand knockdowns?

10
00:00:46.029 --> 00:00:54.589 line:88% align:center
The reflex is to rank by significance — but at two million cells, that breaks down: over 97% of the tested knockdowns clear the bar.

11
00:00:54.589 --> 00:00:57.247 line:88% align:center
So we rank by causal effect size instead.

12
00:00:57.667 --> 00:01:04.377 line:88% align:center
But effect size alone still points at the wrong genes — the biggest hits are the cell's own signaling machinery.

13
00:01:04.377 --> 00:01:10.129 line:88% align:center
So we add what a magnitude ranking leaves out: direction — toward the effector program, or away.

14
00:01:10.129 --> 00:01:14.324 line:88% align:center
Now the machinery falls away, and the candidate brakes rise into view.

15
00:01:14.733 --> 00:01:16.668 line:88% align:center
And this isn't a static picture.

16
00:01:16.668 --> 00:01:26.763 line:88% align:center
Every one of the eleven thousand that passed our testing threshold is here to explore — search any gene, hover any point, and read its causal effect and its direction.

17
00:01:26.763 --> 00:01:28.698 line:88% align:center
It's the real leaderboard, live.

18
00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.321 line:88% align:center
And that's the edge.

19
00:01:30.321 --> 00:01:34.107 line:88% align:center
Differential expression finds correlations — not what to drug.

20
00:01:34.107 --> 00:01:36.978 line:88% align:center
Genetics points to a locus, rarely a direction.

21
00:01:36.978 --> 00:01:44.000 line:88% align:center
We measure what a knockdown actually does, and which way it pushes — then weigh it against genetics and the clinic.

22
00:01:44.433 --> 00:01:58.806 line:88% align:center
From that map, five prior-informed candidates: CBLB, CD5, DGKA, SMAD3, and UBASH3A — each scored across seven lines of evidence, from causal effect and direction to human genetics and clinical precedent.

23
00:01:59.233 --> 00:02:00.371 line:88% align:center
Our lead is CBLB.

24
00:02:00.371 --> 00:02:06.932 line:88% align:center
It's a natural off-switch for T-cell activation, and inhibitors are already in early-phase trials.

25
00:02:06.932 --> 00:02:11.483 line:88% align:center
Its genetics point the same way, and it lands in our brake quadrant.

26
00:02:11.483 --> 00:02:13.023 line:88% align:center
CD5 and DGKA come next.

27
00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:16.348 line:88% align:center
We're honest about what two donors can support.

28
00:02:16.348 --> 00:02:20.317 line:88% align:center
CD5 and DGKA hold up in both; the other three ride on one donor.

29
00:02:20.317 --> 00:02:26.457 line:88% align:center
Known brakes aren't significantly enriched — but that's a two-donor power limit, not a null result.

30
00:02:26.457 --> 00:02:32.535 line:88% align:center
So this stays a ranked shortlist for the full cohort, a hypothesis to test, not a finished answer.

31
00:02:32.967 --> 00:02:39.870 line:88% align:center
Five candidate brakes, led by CBLB — a target the industry already drugs, so recovering it validates our method.

32
00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:46.650 line:88% align:center
Every figure regenerates from cached outputs with one command, checked against a real bug we caught ourselves.

33
00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:52.074 line:88% align:center
Explore the live map, clone the code, and help find the brakes today's drugs still miss.

34
00:02:52.074 --> 00:02:53.676 line:88% align:center
